sprite_sheet "pingpong-art" 1060 x 600 margin 1

machine_manifest "pingpong-art.spritepos" whitespace [meta]/[frames]/[animations]
manifest_frame "name x y w h"
manifest_animation "name fps loop|once frame1 frame2 ..."

image "pingpong-art.png"
format RGBA
alpha "straight alpha, 8-bit per channel"
background transparent
origin top-left (0, 0)
categories "background", "ball-bubble", "bubble-pop", "paddle-cloud"
source "build.py - deterministic Pillow raster art, no external images"

Sheet size: 1060 x 600 px
Margin: 1 px transparent gutters between adjacent sprite frames. The single
background frame is fully opaque; all sprite frames and every area outside the
listed frame rectangles are transparent.

Frame table
-----------
name          x     y     w     h    category
background    260   0     800   600  background
bubble_1      0     0     64    64   ball-bubble
bubble_2      65    0     64    64   ball-bubble
bubble_3      130   0     64    64   ball-bubble
bubble_4      195   0     64    64   ball-bubble
trail_1       0     65    60    24   ball-bubble
trail_2       61    65    60    24   ball-bubble
trail_3       122   65    60    24   ball-bubble
trail_4       183   65    60    24   ball-bubble
cloud_idle    81    90    48    360  paddle-cloud
cloud_hit     130   90    48    360  paddle-cloud
pop_1         0     451   64    64   bubble-pop
pop_2         65    451   64    64   bubble-pop
pop_3         130   451   64    64   bubble-pop
pop_4         195   451   64    64   bubble-pop
pop_5         0     516   64    64   bubble-pop
pop_6         65    516   64    64   bubble-pop
pop_7         130   516   64    64   bubble-pop
pop_8         195   516   64    64   bubble-pop

Layout notes
------------
- The 259 x 450 ball/paddle block occupies x=0..258, y=0..449. Its frame
  rectangles, gutters and coordinates are unchanged from the original pack;
  the contrast revision updates only pixels and descriptive text. The
  background remains appended on the right, so every existing ball/paddle
  source rectangle stays valid exactly as before.
- x=259 is a 1 px fully transparent vertical gutter between the sprite sheet
  and the background.
- The background frame starts at x=260 and covers y=0..599 (800 x 600). It is
  fully opaque (alpha 255 everywhere).
- The bubble-pop block occupies the formerly empty area x=0..258, y=451..579.
  It is two rows of four 64x64 frames in play order: pops 1-4 at y=451 and
  pops 5-8 at y=516, at x=0, 65, 130 and 195. The 1 px separator rows y=450
  and y=515 and the 1 px gutters x=64, 129 and 194 are fully transparent.
- The area below the pop block, x=0..258, y=580..599, is fully transparent.
- Row 1, y=0: four 64x64 bubble frames at x=0, 65, 130 and 195, separated by
  1 px transparent gutters at x=64, 129 and 194.
- Row 2, y=65: four 60x24 trail frames at x=0, 61, 122 and 183, separated by
  1 px transparent gutters at x=60, 121 and 182. The 16 px tail at
  x=243..258 is transparent.
- y=89 is a fully transparent separator row between the bubble block and the
  paddle block.
- Row 3, y=90: two 48x360 paddle frames. The 97 px-wide pair is horizontally
  centered: cloud_idle at x=81, a 1 px gutter at x=129, cloud_hit at x=130.
  The unused sides (x=0..80 and x=178..258) are transparent.
- Every sprite frame keeps at least 2 px of transparent content margin inside
  its frame box. The background is full-bleed and intentionally has no margin.
- All areas outside the listed frame rectangles are transparent.
- Contrast revision: the background uses a deeper periwinkle play band, soft
  blue paddle-lane shading and blue-lavender cloud shadows; the bubble and
  cloud frames carry stronger blue rims. Every original frame rectangle above
  is unchanged; the eight bubble-pop frames were appended below the block.
- Bubble-pop revision: eight 64x64 burst frames continue the idle bubble's
  iridescent white / cyan / lavender film, deep blue inner rim, white specular
  highlight and warm-white sparkles. Render them at 32x32, center anchor,
  play once at 12-14 fps; do not loop.

Authoring source: build.py, a deterministic Python 3 + Pillow renderer. It
regenerates the background and every sprite category from code and packs this
exact layout. No layered-paint or XCF source exists; the script is the source
of truth.
